      "blockId": "lin-sub-blk-1",
      "kind": "explanation",
      "heading": "Substitution Method Steps",
      "content": "Step 1: Express one variable in terms of the other from one equation.\nStep 2: Substitute this value into the other equation to get an equation in one variable.\nStep 3: Solve for the single variable.\nStep 4: Substitute back to obtain the second variable."
    }
  ],
  "workedExamples": [
    {
      "prompt": "Solve the pair of equations 7x - 15y = 2 and x + 2y = 3 by substitution.",
      "steps": [
        "Step 1: From eq 2: x = 3 - 2y.",
        "Step 2: Substitute into eq 1: 7(3 - 2y) - 15y = 2 => 21 - 14y - 15y = 2.",
        "Step 3: 21 - 29y = 2 => -29y = -19 => y = 19/29.",
        "Step 4: x = 3 - 2(19/29) = 3 - 38/29 = (87 - 38)/29 = 49/29."
      ],
      "answer": "x = 49/29, y = 19/29"
    }
  ],
